<title>USA: American Stores keeps expenditure forecast.</title>
<headline>American Stores keeps expenditure forecast.</headline>
<dateline>SALT LAKE CITY 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Stores Co said on Tuesday it was going to keep its 1996 capital expenditures forecast at about $900 million.</p>
<p>American said in a statement it will have opened 100 new stres and remodeled 85 others by the end of the year.</p>
<p>The food and drug retailer reported net income per share at $0.52 for the third quarter ended November 2 against $0.46 the previous year.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
</text>
